{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/748066-pbp-recruitment-hunter-vice-htv-in-1980s-miami","id":748066,"title":"[PBP Recruitment] Hunter Vice: HtV in 1980s Miami","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-01T18:05:37-08:00","id":748066,"title":"[PBP Recruitment] Hunter Vice: HtV in 1980s Miami","content":"Forget New York and Chicago. Forget the goombas in their drab suits and black town cars. The future of criminal enterprise is all about the city of sun. Expensive import convertibles. Perfect ten bodies. Sun and surf. Our erstwhile protagonists are a crew of career criminals. They're nobodies, really, but they've got the two most valuable commodities in this city: youth and ambition. That ambition is clear as the South Beach waters: drugs, money, power, in whichever order is most expedient. What they don't realize is the cost of doing business. It's not just the Haitian heroin wholesalers, the Cuban kingpins, and the emissaries from the Big Five Families. When the sun sets, a new breed of players come out. Red-eyed things in expensive sports coats stalk the neon clubs. Shambling hordes of the once-living in gang colors fight proxy wars in the slums for rival drug lords. Creatures from the abyss fuel competition for the perfect body with infernal pacts that require giving up just a little of yourself in return for a slimmer waist and a bulging bust. The witch-realtor of Palm Shore Estates spent a fortune on his property, and the layout of those new condominiums are aligned to precise geometric patterns. If they want to survive in this city, they'll need to carve out a piece for themselves, through smooth smiles and greased palms or submachine guns and cans of gasoline, probably both.<br /> <br /> While the game wouldn't shy away from the despair of the World of Darkness, it would all be cast under a veneer that mixes the hard-luck weirdo pulp of Elmore Leonard with the glibness of early Tarantino and a dash of Pynchonian oddity.<br /> <br /> So it's not a fully developed idea, but I wanted to see if anyone was interested in the premise, either in the forums here or elsewhere. I'd probably be looking for 3-4 steady players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 11-01-2015, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T13:33:16-08:00","id":752161,"title":"","content":"which Tier the game is going to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:09:50-08:00","id":752345,"title":"","content":"Probably start at tier one and climb over the course of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","